{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548390-dominate-possession","id":1548390,"title":"Dominate ***** Possession","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-10T19:53:27-08:00","id":1548390,"title":"Dominate ***** Possession","content":"As anyone used this, like, really, really used this? How effective was it? I was just thinking, that, a vampire can possess a mortal, at dawn, then, use the mortal to attack the haven of his enemy, during the day-time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T21:06:21-08:00","id":1548395,"title":"","content":"You know that I never had my character ever try it, but it would go against his fraying moral code or has sufficient mastery over the Discipline despite it being an in clan power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T00:56:10-08:00","id":1548397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548390-dominate-possession#post1548390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As anyone used this, like, really, really used this? How effective was it? I was just thinking, that, a vampire can possess a mortal, at dawn, then, use the mortal to attack the haven of his enemy, during the day-time?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has a lot of annoying limitations, at least in VtM20. First, the rolls to activate are two: Charisma + Intimidation at diff. 7 vs the victim's rolling Willpower at diff. 7 (each success of yours beyond the victim's removes one willpower point, and you need to remove them all); then Manipulation + Intimidate at diff. 7 to determine which disciplines you can use. On a pool of 10 dice (assuming you're not an elder but have maximised Manipulation and Intimidate), the average is around 3 successes, limiting you to Auspex and Presence. This means that it can be annoying to pull off but should work on most weak willed humans, assuming that you have invested in the right traits. Finding weak willed humans at dawn requires some planning though, but nothing too bad, unless you get them while they're sleepy.<br /> <br /> Then there is the execution. You're a frail human. All damage you suffer is reflected on your real body, you just get some advantage while soaking. If your possessed body dies, you go into torpor. Your rival's haven is probably hidden, and if he's worth anything, has some daytime defence in place. How you plan to enter the haven and kill your rival makes all the difference, but the fact that you must avoid being injured too severely or killed (because torpor is not nice, especially just after you have attacked someone) is a major drawback.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine used Possession extensively, but I wasn't playing at the time. It worked out for him, but the ST tends to ignore many rules and rolls to keep things flowing, so I don't know if it worked out too well compared to RAW.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T19:17:35-08:00","id":1548416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548390-dominate-possession?p=1548397#post1548397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has a lot of annoying limitations, at least in VtM20. First, the rolls to activate are two: Charisma + Intimidation at diff. 7 vs the victim's rolling Willpower at diff. 7 (each success of yours beyond the victim's removes one willpower point, and you need to remove them all); then Manipulation + Intimidate at diff. 7 to determine which disciplines you can use. On a pool of 10 dice (assuming you're not an elder but have maximised Manipulation and Intimidate), the average is around 3 successes, limiting you to Auspex and Presence. This means that it can be annoying to pull off but should work on most weak willed humans, assuming that you have invested in the right traits. Finding weak willed humans at dawn requires some planning though, but nothing too bad, unless you get them while they're sleepy.<br /> <br /> Then there is the execution. You're a frail human. All damage you suffer is reflected on your real body, you just get some advantage while soaking. If your possessed body dies, you go into torpor. Your rival's haven is probably hidden, and if he's worth anything, has some daytime defence in place. How you plan to enter the haven and kill your rival makes all the difference, but the fact that you must avoid being injured too severely or killed (because torpor is not nice, especially just after you have attacked someone) is a major drawback.<br /> <br /> . . .\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm, well, since I'm getting my material from OG V:tM, someone, must have already tried it, for them to make such complex-rules about it. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T18:17:42-08:00","id":1548647,"title":"","content":"I was reading in Requiem and yes, they say the same thing about going into torpor if you're host is killed and even in Animalism's Possession. However, I don't agree that your PC will die if you're possessing someone and your vampire body gets destroyed; that's what we call a, &quot;Body Thief&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T01:53:05-08:00","id":1548659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548390-dominate-possession?p=1548647#post1548647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading in Requiem and yes, they say the same thing about going into torpor if you're host is killed and even in Animalism's Possession. However, I don't agree that your PC will die if you're possessing someone and your vampire body gets destroyed; that's what we call a, &quot;Body Thief&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But your dominate is powered by your blood.<br /> If your body is destroyed then so is your blood. No more blood, no more power to dominate/possess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T08:59:37-08:00","id":1548675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548390-dominate-possession?p=1548647#post1548647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading in Requiem and yes, they say the same thing about going into torpor if you're host is killed and even in Animalism's Possession. However, I don't agree that your PC will die if you're possessing someone and your vampire body gets destroyed; that's what we call a, &quot;Body Thief&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if you're referring to my comment or another's, but yeah, if your normal body dies while you are in your possessed body (the one you are possessing), you become a body thief. That's not great because you're basically rolling Courage every day and die once you fail, at least in VtM20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T09:00:30-08:00","id":1548676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moriaki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548390-dominate-possession?p=1548659#post1548659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But your dominate is powered by your blood.<br /> If your body is destroyed then so is your blood. No more blood, no more power to dominate/possess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in VtM. In VtM most Dominate powers, including Possession, do not require blood.<br /> <br /> As for Requiem, I would need to check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T01:13:20-08:00","id":1548692,"title":"","content":"The power may not require you to <i>spend </i>blood for it, but I would argue it still needs the power of your vampiric blood. Otherwise any human could use dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T07:17:38-08:00","id":1548702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moriaki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548390-dominate-possession?p=1548692#post1548692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power may not require you to <i>spend </i>blood for it, but I would argue it still needs the power of your vampiric blood. Otherwise any human could use dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just remembered that there are actual rules on what disciplines can be used during Possession. The second roll for this power is to determine just that.<br /> Successes Result 1 success Cannot use Disciplines<br /> 2 successes Can use Auspex and other sensory <br /> powers<br /> 3 successes Can also use Presence and other <br /> powers of emotional manipulation<br /> 4 successes Can also use Dementation, <br /> Dominate, and other powers <br /> of mental manipulation<br /> 5 successes Can also use Chimerstry, <br /> Necromancy, Thaumaturgy, <br /> and other mystical powers \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T07:30:18-08:00","id":1548703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548390-dominate-possession?p=1548702#post1548702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just remembered that there are actual rules on what disciplines can be used during Possession. The second roll for this power is to determine just that.<br /> Successes Result 1 success Cannot use Disciplines<br /> 2 successes Can use Auspex and other sensory<br /> powers<br /> 3 successes Can also use Presence and other<br /> powers of emotional manipulation<br /> 4 successes Can also use Dementation,<br /> Dominate, and other powers<br /> of mental manipulation<br /> 5 successes Can also use Chimerstry,<br /> Necromancy, Thaumaturgy,<br /> and other mystical powers \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the RAW. I would personally prefer a system, inspired by Requiem 2E, though I can't remember how it works there in detail, where <i>all</i> Disciplines are powered by the Beast. The result is that I would allow the use of physical Disciplines and not only mental ones, and that the clan disciplines (Vigor, Celerity, Resilience, Animalism, Dominate, Auspex, Majesty, Protean, Obfuscate, Nightmare) are all usable, or maybe they are usable if enough successes are scored, but not through some hierarchy.<br /> <br /> The idea is that it is not the vampiric body in itself to hold the power, but it's the Beast that takes over the body and empowers it in strange ways. So if the soul - Beast included - is transferred in another body, the Beast can use its powers in that body too provided that the grip is solid enough. Blood Potency alone and the natural benefits of all vampires would be missing because the link with this body is not complete and is not adapted to vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T02:07:12-08:00","id":1548727,"title":"","content":"RAW, generational limits still play.<br /> If Mithras were to succeed in taking total control of Monty Coven's body, he would still be limited by Monty's generation/blood and be unable to use lvl 9 disciplines.<br /> Admittedly not the same situation but the same 'logic' applies, the mind (or beast if you will) takes over the body.<br /> If it doesn't depend on the blood then why would he even bother with a vampiric body?<br /> Therefor I've always found allowing to use disciplines while possessing a human/animal body makes no sense. But then again so do a lot of other RAW.<br /> I tend to roll with it, it's fantasy after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T20:25:20-08:00","id":1548744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moriaki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548390-dominate-possession?p=1548727#post1548727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, generational limits still play.<br /> If Mithras were to succeed in taking total control of Monty Coven's body, he would still be limited by Monty's generation/blood and be unable to use lvl 9 disciplines.<br /> Admittedly not the same situation but the same 'logic' applies, the mind (or beast if you will) takes over the body.<br /> If it doesn't depend on the blood then why would he even bother with a vampiric body?<br /> Therefor I've always found allowing to use disciplines while possessing a human/animal body makes no sense. But then again so do a lot of other RAW.<br /> I tend to roll with it, it's fantasy after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the same logic applies. First, RAW, generational limits <i>don't </i>play. If I have Auspex 9 e succeed in possessing a mortal using Possession and score 2 successes on the roll to determine which disciplines I can use, I can use all 9 dots of Auspex.<br /> Second, Mithras and Monty Coven's situation is different because it's not Possession at all. Mithras has been diablerised but his mental might was such that he took over Monty Coven's body instead of his soul being destroyed. This is an issue with diablerie that's mentioned in many manuals but never got a proper and clear system, but it is different from Dominate because it's not a discipline at all, but some kind of quirk of very old and strong willed vampires, who may or may not know Dominate. It makes sense that it would play out differently, including extra limits: in theory the mathuselah should be dead. Instead he managed to survive, but with a power loss. Depending on who diablerised him and the benefits of this new identity, this may not be a significant problem, or it may even be to the mathuselah's advantage, but I don't think it should be compared to any of the Discipline powers. It makes perfect sense that using a discipline would yield less trouble and limitations than merely partially surviving a diablerie because of how mighty one's ancient will is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-24T00:51:42-08:00","id":1548748,"title":"","content":"Apologies, when I wrote RAW, I was not referring to the dominate/possession rule specific, but rather Rules As Written in general. Bad penmanship from my part.<br /> The fact that it's not dominate/possession does not change the logic of having to depend on the power of the blood.<br /> The rules about dominate/possession do seem to contradict this, but they look to be a not well thought out exception (to me).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}